    "abstract": "Illustrated parts figure for the thrust lever quadrant, its detent seal and the friction clamp assembly, stating why the seal is not an aircraft-level replacement and why the two clamp standards are never mixed.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "This figure identifies the thrust lever quadrant detent seal, the friction clamp, the clamp mounting bracket and the anchor hardware inside the centre pedestal.",
      "figure_note": "The quadrant is supplied as an exchange assembly and the internal items are shown for identification only; individual replacement of the detent seal on the aircraft is not permitted because the breakout force must be set on the bench, and a seal changed in the pedestal leaves the force unmeasured and unset. That is the reason the obvious short cut is closed off, and the sentence is quoted verbatim in the operator communication that accompanies the exchange programme. The bonded-face friction clamp and the fluorosilicone seal are supplied together and must not be mixed with the earlier items: the earlier clamp facing takes up the migrating lubricant that the new seal is meant to keep out."
    },
